        "*The target is a defined rule, not an observed outcome: trend_direction == 'down' — a threshold applied to the comparison between the last 30 days and the previous 30 days of impressions. The model is trained on this label, but rather than predicting a flat yes/no, it outputs a probability — a float between 0 and 1 — which is what makes ranking possible in the first place. That probability is then blended with the rule-based baseline into the final scoring system used to rank pages for review.*"
