      "source": [
        "## 3. Success metric\n",
        "\n",
        "*Precision@K is the best fit here: of the top K ranked pages, how many are actually true positives. Restricting to a fixed K matters — measuring precision across the entire dataset would include thousands of pages no reviewer will ever get to, so it wouldn't reflect what's practically usable. I'll use K=50 (matching the starter model's reported Precision@50), since the docs don't specify an exact review-team capacity; the goal is to maximize how many of the pages a reviewer has time for are ones genuinely worth reviewing.*"
